# "Until end of turn" (CR 514.2): the animation ends in cleanup, and the Core is a Kindred Artifact with no power or
# toughness again (the 4/4 was only its base while the effect lasted). It has every creature type still but is no
# creature, so Bot2's Shoot the Sheriff has no legal target in it on turn 4 (refused), while Ornithopter, a creature,
# remains the legal control. Bot1 animates the Core on turn 3 (the setup of firdoch-core-animated-is-an-outlaw-and-
# keeps-its-own-types), and checks it was a 4/4 creature that turn.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Sol Ring
Firdoch Core
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Shoot the Sheriff
Swamp
Swamp
Swamp x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Firdoch Core.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Firdoch Core.Activate(Ability: {4})
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp#2.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Firdoch Core.Types = Kindred; Artifact; Creature
? Bot1.Battlefield.Firdoch Core.Power = 4
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
! Bot2.Hand.Shoot the Sheriff.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Firdoch Core)
Bot2.Hand.Shoot the Sheriff.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Firdoch Core.Types = Kindred; Artifact
Bot1.Battlefield.Firdoch Core.Subtypes = (every creature type)
Bot1.Battlefield.Firdoch Core.Power = (absent)
Bot2.Graveyard = Shoot the Sheriff; Ornithopter
